    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass (there's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, which includes the new GOLD tier check).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` is `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the established pattern used for `namesakeCount` (a create-time snapshot persisted on the entity and read by the mapper), I:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`: counts owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` after this create (the persisted, backfilled members plus the not-yet-saved new owner; owners with no household get size 1) and stores it on the entity.\n\n2. **Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `household-size` step right after `household-id` (`AssignHousehold`), so the shared `householdId` is already assigned and existing members backfilled before counting, and before `save`. It carries `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the `householdSize` field mapped to a new `household_size` column, with getter/setter.\n\n4. **Schemas** \u2014 added `household_size INTEGER` to the owners table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Tests run on hsqldb.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` expression to return `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falling through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nBecause the size is a snapshot captured at create time (not recomputed at read), it correctly reflects \"3 or more members **after this create**\" per the specification.",
