    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change follows the codebase's established conventions closely and puts each piece of logic in the natural unit.\n\n- **New function class fits the sibling pattern exactly.** `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` mirrors `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` (and `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`, `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning`): one derived field per `AssignOwner*` step, `service(@Val Owner, OwnerRepository)`, same `findAll().stream().filter(...).count()` shape, same in-place mutation of the `@Val Owner`. A maintainer would find this immediately familiar.\n- **Right unit / no over-consolidation.** Even though `AssignHousehold` also iterates `findAll()`, this codebase deliberately keeps each derived attribute in its own step rather than piling them into one class. Keeping household-size separate is the idiomatic choice, and its Javadoc correctly documents the ordering dependency on `AssignHousehold` (backfill of `householdId` must happen first), which the YAML wiring respects (`household-id \u2192 household-size`).\n- **Tier logic stays in the mapper.** GOLD is layered in front of the existing SILVER/BRONZE ternary, matching the existing convention of deriving `membershipTier` from owner fields in `OwnerMapper` rather than scattering it into a function. Not a new catch-all.\n- **Additive, consistent supporting changes.** Model field + getter/setter match the `namesakeCount` precedent; all four DB schemas and the OpenAPI description are updated coherently; the new step is transaction-governed like its neighbors.\n\nNothing is duplicated or misplaced.",
